    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d205">

                <pb facs="0474" n="348" xml:id="pg348"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515PC/6a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Chile</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Collier</hi>)<anchor n="41" xml:id="d205-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-03-23T13:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 23,
                                1925—1 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>12. Inform Chilean authorities that the President has today appointed General
                    John J. Pershing as President of the Plebiscitary Commission. The Department
                    hopes to be able to advise you in a few days of the President’s nominee on the
                    Special Commission to determine the boundaries of Tacna-Arica.<anchor n="42"
                        xml:id="d205-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d205-f1" n="41" type="source" xml:id="d205-f1-content">
                <p>The same, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi>, to the Ambassador in
                    Peru, as Department’s telegram No. 21 (file No. 723.2515PC/9a).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d205-f2" n="42" xml:id="d205-f2-content">
                <p>By telegrams of Mar. 27, 5 p.m., the Ambassadors in Chile and Peru were
                    instructed to inform the Governments to which they were accredited that Gen. Jay
                    J. Morrow, U. S. Army (retired), ex-Governor of the Panama Canal Zone, had been
                    appointed American member of the Special Boundary Commission (file No.
                    723.2515PC/15a,b).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
